(MATCH SCORING EXPLAINED \(PLAIN ENGLISH\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Source file: src/utils/matchScoring.js) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This document explains two different outputs the app can compute for a hike or event:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Match score: a straight average of how close each preference is \(0% to 100%\).) Tj
T*
(- Cosine similarity: a content-based score using a feature vector and angle math.) Tj
T*
(They often move together, but they are not the same thing. The match score is a simple) Tj
T*
(average. Cosine similarity looks at the overall shape of the user vs event vectors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1\) WHAT DATA IS USED) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(User preferences: experience level, preferred difficulty, preferred duration, budget range,) Tj
T*
(preferred trail type, preferred distance, preferred elevation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Event details: difficulty \(or distance/elevation/duration if difficulty is missing\),) Tj
T*
(duration, price, trail type \(and text description\), distance, elevation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2\) HOW EACH PERCENT IS CALCULATED) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each parameter becomes a percent from 0.00 to 1.00 \(0% to 100%\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Difficulty \(experience + preferred difficulty\): both labels are mapped to an index in the) Tj
T*
(  order Beginner, Intermediate, Technical, Expert. If the gap is 0, percent = 1. If the gap) Tj
T*
(  is 1, percent = 1 - 1/3 = 0.6667. If the gap is 2, percent = 0.3333. If the gap is 3,) Tj
T*
(  percent = 0.) Tj
T*
(- Duration / Distance / Elevation: percent = 1 - |actual - preferred| / max\(actual,) Tj
T*
(  preferred\). Exact match gives 1.00. Farther away lowers the percent.) Tj
T*
(- Budget: the text range is parsed into numbers. The cap is max if present, else min, else) Tj
T*
(  midpoint. If price is at or below the cap, percent = 1. If price is above, percent = cap /) Tj
T*
(  price.) Tj
T*
(- Trail type: if the user has a preferred trail type, the event gets 1 if it matches the) Tj
T*
(  event's trailType or appears in its description; otherwise 0. If the user did not set a) Tj
T*
(  preference, this value is null and is not averaged.) Tj
T*
(3\) FINAL MATCH SCORE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(All non-null percents are averaged with equal weight. Missing user preferences \(null values\)) Tj
T*
(are ignored rather than treated as 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4\) COSINE SIMILARITY \(CONTENT-BASED\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cosine similarity uses a numeric vector for the user and the event. Each number is) Tj
T*
(normalized to 0..1. Numeric values are scaled by caps: duration/12, distance/40,) Tj
T*
(elevation/2000, price/12000. Difficulty labels are mapped to scores \(beginner=0.2,) Tj
T*
(intermediate=0.6, technical=1, expert=1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(User vector order:) Tj
ET
endstream
